    {
      "q": "How much does Science Applications International make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Science Applications International has $3.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Science Applications International won 938 awards so far this fiscal year at an average award size of $3.8M, and obligations are down 18.9% year over year. Science Applications International’s current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Science Applications International?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer from Science Applications International with $1.4B in FY2026 obligations. The General Services Administration follows with $1.2B, and other top buyers include the Department of Homeland Security ($259M), Department of the Treasury ($188M), and Department of State ($127M)."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Science Applications International sell to the government?",
